(SentinelChain is a credible full-stack supplier-risk monitoring MVP with strong product completeness and clear business relevance. Across code) Tj
T* (and PPT, the strongest throughline is practical decision support: dashboards, supplier drill-downs, alerts, simulations, reports, logistics views, and) Tj
T* (admin governance are all aligned to procurement risk management. The backend appears thoughtfully organized around domain routes and) Tj
T* (services, with auth, RBAC, audit logging, realtime updates, and centralized server-side LLM usage. On the AI side, the team implemented) Tj
T* (grounded prompts tied to live supplier and alert context, not just generic chatbot behavior, and used LLMs in multiple workflows that map directly) Tj
T* (to user value: explanation, report drafting, and what-if narrative generation. Security and HITL are also better than average for a hackathon build,) Tj
T* (especially the admin approval gate for scoring/model changes.) Tj
ET
